2,Echoes of Papa Nui — Ancient Rapa Nui Music - YouTubeAustronesian Music - YouTubeAustronesian Soundscapes: Performing Arts in Oceania and ...Performing Austronesia in the Twenty-first Century: A Rapa ...Rapa Nui Cultural Songbook CollectionSinging and Survival: The Music of Easter Island.,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=q0mVwkco4Ro,"The haunting, rhythmic qualities of Rapa Nui music come from traditional chanting styles, the use of vocal harmonies, and natural percussion instruments like stones and wooden drums. Austronesian culture includes more than 1200 ethnic groups, across South Asia, Southeast Asia, Taiwan, the Philippines, parts of China, as well as the Pacific as far afield as the Maori in New ... It does not seem particularly handy at first glance: The area where people who speak Austronesian languages live covers a huge amount of the globe’s surface from Madagascar to Rapa Nui, making it a seemingly elusive category of reference. In this way, contemporary Rapa Nui performers have forged meaningful contact with indigenous performers in places like Taiwan and Borneo, far removed from Polynesia but linked by an ancient shared Austronesian heritage. The Rapa Nui Songbook features a collection of songs that celebrate the culture, history, and beauty of Rapa Nui (Easter Island). The lyrics express themes of love, connection to ancestors, nature, and the importance of community and tradition. Apr 7, 2021 · This history and ethnography of music on the island of Rapa Nui (Easter Island, Isla de Pascua) highlights not just cultural survival, but cultural thriving, through the decimation of a population, centuries of imperialist exploitation, and their aftermath.",Rapa,Austronesian
